 Paired with tender and fluffy rice, the dish left me with only one word in my mind—\"delicious\". \n\nSo I couldn't resist having another serving:)\n<color=Highlight>Jewel Boba</color>, rating: ☆☆☆☆\nI found myself longing for more as I savored the delightful Jewel Boba, each sip leaving me yearning for another taste. If I had a second stomach dedicated solely to desserts, there's no doubt it would be reserved for the delicious dessert soup offered here in Jinzhou.. And if I were to recommend just one, Jewel Boba would undoubtedly be my top choice. Boasting over thirty years of renowned excellence, this sweet treat remains as delicious and affordable as ever.\nDuring my visit, I ordered the new buy-one-get-one-free dessert soup. The owner told me that its launch was inspired by a happy couple celebrating their anniversary at the shop—the owner, pleased with their happiness, presented them with a specially made drink. As the couple highly praised its taste, the owner decided to share its taste to more customers. After listening to this warm story, I, who was holding two cups alone, couldn't shake the bitterness of coming here alone. Luckily, the sweetness of the Jewel Boba somewhat lifted my spirits.\n<color=Highlight>Liuxian Teahouse</color>, rating: ☆☆☆☆\nLiuxian Teahouse boasts its Bittberry Tea with distinctive bitterness, which forces you to question everything with a single sip. However, beneath the initial shock, a subtle sweetness emerges, with great persistence in the mouth. \nUnlike the bustling Panhua's Restaurant, Liuxian Teahouse provides a tranquil atmosphere where one can recline in a chair, fan in hand, and while away the hours immersed in the peaceful embrace of life unfolding around them.\n<color=Highlight>Borderland Cuisine</color>, rating: ☆☆☆☆☆\n...",
   "InfoDisplay_10900007_Title": "Mochelin Dining Guide: Tasty Jinzhou - Food Exploration",
-  "InfoDisplay_10900008_Text": "Loong Buns, Jinzhou Stew, Star Flakes... Before delving into the numerous specialties of Jinzhou, let me introduce you to a time-honored dish—\"Rising Loong\".\n\n<color=Highlight>Rising Loong</color>, rating: ☆☆☆☆☆\n\nFor anyone exploring Jinzhou, tasting Rising Loong is a must. The dish presents itself with a captivating golden crispiness, with its preparation involving intricate steps to reproduce the scene where a carp looks up to the sky, aspiring to become a dragon. This dish narrates the awakening of Jué. Back then, countless carps leaped from the water to pay homage to it. It is an event seem auspicious by Jinzhou people. Therefore, if you seek good fortune, don't miss the chance to savor Rising Loong!\n\n\n\n<color=Highlight>Food Ration Bar</color>, rating: ☆☆☆\n\nAlthough I've given it only three stars, the significance of Food Ration Bar goes beyond its taste. Its major characteristic lies in its convenience, accessibility, and ample nutritional value, making it available for every soldier who fights bravely and relentlessly on the frontlines.\n\nMore importantly, each Food Ration Bar comes with a note, expressing Jinzhou people's thoughts, wishes, and gratitude to the soldiers who safeguard the peace and prosperity of Jinzhou.\n\nEven though countless challenges may lie ahead, Jinzhou and its people consistently stand in support of the soldiers. The soldiers courageously protect Jinzhou with their lives, and in return, Jinzhou becomes their steadfast shield.",
